            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Pamela Emerson"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used Ghirardelli cocoa powder and changed that from 1/4 to 1/3 cup. I also changed the Peanut butter from 1/2 to 3/4 cup. I added 1/4 tsp of peanut butter extract made by Lorann. The cookies were fabulous",
            "datePublished": "2021-09-08T03:16:32.083Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Liliane Sparkes"
            },
            "reviewBody": "haha so this is sort of a different recipee a bit..\n\nI reduced to 1 1/2 cups of sugar (half of it xylitol), double the cocoa, to 1/2 cup, I had no milk so I used 1/2c cream and then reduced the butter to a little over 1/4c. Then I used extra vanilla, and....\n\n used corn flakes instead of oatmeal (this is the only mistake, maybe they were too old or maybe the heat sort of cooked them so they have an odd texture)\n\nOverall they are great!! You really can't taste the xylitol so next time I might use even more xylitol than sugar, and also keep the xylitol/sugar combo to 1 cup ( I find them really sweet even at 1 1/2 cup) . I am waiting for them to cool...sort of ;)",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-18T22:11:07.930Z"
          },
          {
